      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In this retrospective study, ten patients with lumbar iatrogenic instability are reported who were treated by pedicular fixation and bone grafting with an average follow-up of 18 months. Early results, which are mostly encouraging, show relief of symptoms, solid fusion of spine, and maintenance of lumbar curve with no major complications."},
